---
description: |
  Writes the latest version of every TruePattern Sigma rule into one
  multi-document YAML file for the `sigma` operator.

  Run the operator on a complete walk of the feed: it replaces the file with
  the rules of its input, so a partial input, such as from an `added_after`
  poll, would remove all other rules. The operator writes nothing if its input
  contains no Sigma rule.

  Every rule must be a single YAML document. The operator removes a leading
  preamble of blank lines, comments, and one document marker, as well as a
  final document end marker. It skips rules with several YAML documents, such
  as correlation rules, and warns about each one. It also skips rules whose YAML does
  not parse, because the `sigma` operator ignores the complete file if one
  document fails to parse. If several rules
  share a Sigma rule ID, it keeps the most recently modified one, because the
  `sigma` operator ignores all rules with a duplicate ID.

  The operator forwards the STIX Indicators of the rules that it wrote, so that
  you can continue with `truepattern::ocsf::normalize` and
  `truepattern::update_context`.
args:
  named:
    - name: path
      type: string
      description: The rule file to write, such as `/var/lib/tenzir/truepattern/sigma.yaml`.
---

where type == "indicator" and pattern_type == "sigma"
truepattern::latest
// Normalizes the rule to a single document without a leading preamble of
// blank lines, comments, and one document marker, and without a final
// document end marker.
_text = pattern.replace("\r\n", "\n")
_text = _text.replace_regex(r"^([ \t]*(#[^\n]*)?\n)*(---[ \t]*(#[^\n]*)?(\n|$))?", "")
// A final document end marker, followed only by blank lines, ends the rule.
_text = _text.replace_regex(r"\n\.\.\.[ \t]*(#[^\n]*)?(\n[ \t]*)*$", "\n")
// Any remaining document marker at the start of a line separates documents.
assert not _text.match_regex(r"(?m)^(---|\.\.\.)([ \t#]|$)"),
  message=f"skipping Sigma rule {id}: not a single YAML document"
_rule = _text.parse_yaml()
where _rule != null
// The latest version comes first, so `deduplicate` keeps it.
deduplicate _rule.id? else id
drop _rule
// A stable order keeps the documents in place across updates.
sort id
fork {
  summarize rules=collect(_text)
  where rules.length() > 0
  this = {text: rules.join("\n---\n")}
  // The operator writes the file in one go after the walk completes.
  to_file $path {
    write_lines
  }
}
drop _text
